 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Light for «يستغفر», geometric for Allah's names. 112:1-5: the tafsirs differ on «خطيئة» (Al-Muyassar: unintended; As-Sa'di: a major sin), so it is not glossed. No people drawn, no motif on the blamed acts. STAGING v4: 109: a small group of men (3, no woman) gathers in a town at dusk, the ones who argued for the treacherous in this world (both tafsirs); no speech arcs, so nobody speaks toward an empty side (the occasion of revelation, the accused and the stolen goods are not drawn); an hourglass plate for the Day (109:12-13), nothing literal. 110: a man enters, lowers his head on 110:7 (returning in regret, Al-Muyassar) and raises his hands on 110:8 (seeking forgiveness); light plate, geometric for the closing names. 111-112: two men in a market; no blamed act is drawn; on 112:7 the wrongdoer points at the other man (casting his sin on an innocent, both tafsirs), the camera holds on the innocent on 112:9 and on the slanderer on 112:11; no reaction is invented for the innocent. Geometric over 111:9-11."
 },
